From 902b83fb28a11ab9b34bcfa1c0ccdc4355ad4311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:15:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 80/97] recoverssm: allow pipeline parallelism for Qwen4Exp on
 the V2 runner

Upstream RecoverSSM commits a step in the same step's postprocess, hence PP=1. Under pipeline parallelism a
non-last rank learns a step's accepted counts only when the PP broadcast arrives pp_size steps later, while later
builds overwrite the persistent commit inputs. The commit is now deferred with its own copy of those inputs, and
the PP=1 check is lifted for Qwen4Exp on Model Runner V2. Config and CPU tests cover the deferral.
